8	\chapter{Physics problem IPhO\_2026\_1\_C\_1}
9	\label{ch:IPhO2026Problems_problem_IPhO_2026_1_C_1}
10	
11	\paragraph{Problem source.}
12	A photon of angular frequency omega is absorbed by an ozone molecule O3 at rest,
13	dissociating it into O2 and O.  Let U\_i and U\_f be the ground-state energies of
14	O3 and O2 and define Delta U = U\_f - U\_i.  The outgoing O2 momentum makes angle
15	theta with the incident photon.  Treat the oxygen fragments classically and
16	non-relativistically, take the mass of an oxygen atom to be m, and use photon
17	momentum p\_gamma = E\_gamma/c = hbar*omega/c.
18	
19	Current subquestion:
20	Determine the minimum angular frequency omega\_min required for dissociation at outgoing O2 angle theta, in terms of hbar, c, theta, Delta U, and m.
21	
22	\paragraph{Current subquestion.}
23	Determine the minimum angular frequency omega\_min required for dissociation at outgoing O2 angle theta, in terms of hbar, c, theta, Delta U, and m.
24	
25	\paragraph{Recorded answer/context.}
26	For theta <= pi/2, omega\_min = 3*m*c\textasciicircum{}2*[1 - sqrt(1 - (Delta U/(3*m*c\textasciicircum{}2))*(2*sin(theta)\textasciicircum{}2 + 1))]/[hbar*(2*sin(theta)\textasciicircum{}2 + 1)]. For theta >= pi/2 use the same threshold evaluated at theta = pi/2.
